                                "example_id": "175d822d-3202-4d45-9b5c-c727d77c9f8e",
                                "sense_id": "7f9c5d2b-4970-3546-842e-4876840875e1",
                                "text": "The flagon of wine and the Wardon pie, what have they come to? Vin ordinaire in a wooden mug, and a quashy mess of baking pears under a pie-crust of the middle ages?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "747e71b3-f782-4f9c-a4fb-c4779b949eb4",
                                "sense_id": "7f9c5d2b-4970-3546-842e-4876840875e1",
                                "text": "The rock on which the jong stands must at one time have been lapped by the waters of the lake, but at the present time the Yam-dok tso has retreated so far, that a quashy stretch of vivid green quagmire spreads between the road and the shore."
                            }
